 - Condensed slot hardening: hand-drawn explicit H are stripped before storing condensed (the overlay adds implicit H itself, so kept H would double-render); expanded generation unchanged (strip → linearize → top up).
 - V2000 counts-line located by shape, not position: JSME depict output uses a 2-line header (counts at index 2) vs 3-line stored files — `fParseMolV2000` (plus `fMakeAnnotatedSkeletal` and the horizontal-equivalent chain check) now scans for the counts line instead of hardcoding index 3. Without this every JSME rung failed validation and the ladder always fell through to drawn geometry.
 - Depict layout-race fix: `fMolDraftDepictSmiles` is now async — inputs once, then polls `molFile()` (up to 6 reads × 120ms) until the output parses with the drawn heavy-atom count, instead of a same-tick read that caught JSME mid-layout (truncated ~151-char stubs, `heavy 9 vs 0`). `fMolDraftAccept` is async (sole caller is a fire-and-forget `onclick`, so safe); `fParseMolV2000` additionally fails closed on truncated input (body-length check, non-empty element fields, no phantom `C@(0,0)`). Cache-busters bumped to `?v=54.3` so mixed old/new file versions can't recur. Verified live: the `display(canon)` rung now wins via read-until-stable (`depict settled`, `skelSrc=display`), builtin remains as fallback.
+- 2D bond-length vars (hardcoded, owner-tuned): `MOLGEN_CC_LEN = 1.0` (all heavy–heavy bonds in every slot) + `MOLGEN_CH_LEN = 0.5` (half of C–C, against branched-alkyl H overlap) in `core-54.js`; linearizer, zigzag and expanded H top-up read them (was: hardcoded `1.17` / `0.78`). Headless-verified: linearized + zigzag C–C uniform at CC, topped-up H all at CH. Stored 141 keep their geometry. Headless H–H overlap sweep (141 regen-expanded MOLs, non-vicinal H pairs): CH=0.5 least-bad (worst 0.170, 3 complex branched offenders) vs 0.004–0.156 at 0.55–0.78; stored hand layouts clean (min 0.321) — residual collisions are bisection *placement* on canonical orthogonal layouts, not length; collision-aware placement queued as the real fix. Cache-busters `?v=54.5`.
+- Per-mode C–C pixel equalizer (`molview-54.js`): JSME rescales each loaded MOL by whole-input bond statistics (measured: uniform MOLs render 1.40 regardless of stored scale — butane 0.825→1.40, customs 0.10→1.40; mixed heavy+H MOLs inflate: expanded 2.17–2.36), so expanded rendered bigger C–C than condensed from identical stored skeletons. New `fMol2DModeScaleFactor()` (= meanAllBonds/meanHeavyBonds of the loaded MOL, 1.0 when heavy-only) feeds `fMol2DModeScale()`/`fApplyMol2DScale()`; all display scale writes (`fLoadMol2D`, `fReapplyZoomScale2D`, both scenario apply sites) route through it — user zoom stays in `molZoom2D`, factor recomputes per load, nothing stored. Expanded-only label compensation (`fApplyMol2DFont()`, boot base 9, clamp 7–20, reset elsewhere): the scaled-down view shrinks atom labels with it, so the font counter-scales to condensed pixel size; set before `readMolFile` in `fLoadMol2D` (first paint correct) and re-asserted on every scale write. Same treatment for overlay numbering (`fShowNumbering`: font 380→380/factor clamp 296–844, stroke + anchors scaled, expanded only; other modes byte-identical output). Collision-aware H placement (`fGenExpandedMol` + `MOLGEN_H_MINSEP = 0.4`): each new H tries angular gaps largest-first and takes the first clearing 0.4 against placed non-vicinal atoms (maximin fallback); clean molecules keep byte-identical coords, only colliding placements move. Symmetric-splay refinement: when the offender is a placed H, both rotate ±δ (equal/opposite, bond lengths kept) so each stays near its ideal sector instead of one jumping sides. Headless sweep: CH=0.5 global min 0.404 with zero sub-0.25 pairs; with splay ALL of 0.5–0.78 clear 0.4 (0.55→0.413, 0.6→0.443, 0.65→0.455, 0.7→0.403, 0.78→0.404). Headless-verified under the depict model: every expanded test case equalizes to exactly 1.40 (condensed level); methane-style H-only MOLs fall back to 1.0. Edit-applet/draft-preview scale writes untouched (true coords there). Cache-busters `?v=54.12`.
+- New ignores the 2D radio (always full triple generation; heavy skeleton linearized at Accept so hand lengths land on `MOLGEN_CC_LEN`); Edit updates only the edited slot in place on same-molecule redraws (history `updated-slot:<variant>`, siblings byte-untouched; skeletal still via ladder, never verbatim). Fork ⇒ full generation (New always + Edit-different: `drawnVariant` ignored, linearize → top-up → ladder; outcome-based, not entry-based). Edit producing a different molecule asks via confirm ("fork as new", stored source untouched). Edit skips auto-tidy (custom deltas survive Submit→Accept verbatim; manual Linearize stays explicit). Stray-H guard at Edit-expanded Accept (H32 class: flags H beyond 1.75× the drawing's min H-bond + unbonded H; 0/141 stored expanded flagged, H32 synthetic flags exactly). Draft bar names the contract at entry + preview (same/different hint). Cache-busters `?v=54.12`.
+- OpenClatura second oracle, Phase 1 (display only): `fFetchIUPAC_OC` (`iupac-54.js`, `/name?smiles=` + `format=json`, parser verified live against CCO/benzene/garbage incl. 422 shape; single attempt, fail-soft, no bulk) feeds an "IUPAC (OpenClatura)" row (OPSIN status shown only when unmatched) in the molecule info panel (select-time fetch via `fLogMolSelectWithOC`, cached on entry, molecule-guarded repaint) and in the draft preview (post-PubChem, canonical-first SMILES — speaks on no-record amber drafts), persisted as `openclaturaEN`/`openclaturaOpsin` on accepted customs (saved files carry it; header untouched). Verbatim display only — no verdicts, no auto-correction (Phase 2: shared-comparator second verdict). 4 new lang keys (labels identical GR/EN; `molInfoOCMissing`/`draftOCFetching` translated). Cache-busters `?v=54.13`.
