+- Merged display verdicts (owner choice): OC accepted as valid even against PubChem — draft auto-check is OR (PubChem 3-way via shared `fMolDraftPCMatch` helper, or OC `fMatchENvsOC`; untouched-only; source recorded as `enAutoSource` in `nameCheck` + save-file header), both oracle rows carry read-only ✓/✕/? glyphs (`draftPCMatchTip`/`draftPCMismatchTip` added), name panel stays untinted when either oracle agrees (red only on disagreement, amber/lavender rules unchanged), green OC-match badge removed (match = quiet; mismatch/missing badges stay). Batch REVIEW tables stay per-oracle; GR untouched. Cache-busters `?v=54.15`.
+- Stale-marker fix: each oracle completion hook recomputes both markers (`fMulerOCFetchDone` re-runs the PubChem apply first so a build-time red clears once OC data lands; `fMulerENFetchDone` re-asserts the OC marker whose tooltip the PubChem repaint would wipe). Cache-busters `?v=54.16`.
+- Draft hardening + engine strictness (2026-11-06): Accept gains `_epoch`/`_submitId` guards + `accepting` re-entrancy block (no ghost Accept after Cancel during depict polls; Draw mid-fetch invalidates in-flight oracle/3D so the old drawing's oracle never paints the new canvas); fork/stray-H confirm callbacks re-validate identity and release the lock. Oracle HTML injection closed (`fMolDraftEsc` now escapes `"'`; verdict tips + bar labels escaped). Depict restore routes through `fApplyMol2DScale()` (no scale/font drift after skeletal rungs); sandbox sync uses the equalizer too. Inline-SDF loader rejects `end "model.sdf"` terminator lines and surfaces the pending-3D path when JSmol is not live instead of recording an invisible 3D model. Engine: `fGuessNameEN_simple` honors all 20 stems (was `>10`), `EN_ALKYL`/`EN_MULTIPREFIX` extended to C20, `MOLGEN_*` frozen to `const` (divergent `typeof` fallbacks removed), `MOLGEN_STDVALENCE` adds S:2/P:3, `fParseMolV2000` fails closed on non-finite coords and drops (not coerces) bond orders outside 1..3. Fork-accepted customs now set `openclaturaDone` like the update path.
