+- Linearizer overlap fix (2026-11-06): `fLinearizeMol` gave every extra fork the identical +90° rotation, so two methyls of one tert-butyl centre landed in perfect overlap; adjacent bulky branches compounded it. Extras now alternate +90°/-90° then ±45° diagonal relief (length-preserving), chain neighbours stagger opposite sides (isolated branches unchanged), and an occupancy guard (`LIN_MINSEP = 0.3×CC`, claimed + placed) with pop-time recheck falls through to the next free angle — clean molecules keep byte-identical coords, only colliding placements move. Verified on a synthetic adjacent-di-tert-butyl graph (min non-vicinal heavy–heavy distance 0 → 1.0×CC).
 
